--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-003-use-exact-hour-intervals-for-short-rentals.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-use-exact-hour-intervals-for-short-rentals
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use exact-hour intervals for short rentals"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The desk needs to support afternoon rentals while preserving the established daily-rental and discount
+model.
+
+## Decision
+
+Accept rental and availability boundaries only on exact UTC hours. A period with both boundaries at
+midnight is a whole-day rental and continues to use the daily price. A non-midnight period must be
+shorter than 24 hours and uses the item's optional hourly price for each elapsed hour. Reject periods
+of 24 hours or more that do not use midnight boundaries.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Hourly bookings retain half-open overlap behavior, so back-to-back rentals are available. An item
+without an hourly price cannot be rented for a short hourly period. Long-rental discounts remain
+limited to whole-day rentals.
